# BuildKit uses this file instead of the root .dockerignore for
# Dockerfile.pawchat, so it must repeat everything the root file excludes.
#
# The root .dockerignore leaves a local `target/` and `node_modules/` in the
# build context (they don't exist on a fresh CI checkout, so it only ever hurt
# local builds — over 1 GB of context transfer before compilation even starts).
#
# `.git` is deliberately NOT excluded: crates/lib/build.rs shells out to git to
# stamp GIT_HASH into the binary.

**/target
target
**/node_modules
node_modules

# we do our own version pinning in the Dockerfile
rust-toolchain.toml
